`createOpportunityActionValidator` (length 642, result level `warning`). Per `sniffs/bundle/validators.json::createOpportunityActionValidator`:

```
if (pipeline_id) {
  push { resource: "pipeline", field: "pipeline_id", value: pipeline_id }
  if (pipeline_stage_id) {
    push { resource: "pipeline_stage", field: "pipeline_stage_id",
           value: pipeline_stage_id, context: { pipelineId: pipeline_id } }
  }
} else {
  push { field: "pipeline_id", message: "pipeline_required" }
}

for each f in fields:
  if (f.field) push { resource: "opp_custom_field", field: f.field, ... }
```

Two existence lookups: `pipeline` and `pipeline_stage` (the latter is contextualized by the parent `pipelineId`). Every entry is `result: "warning"` — the builder's validator never blocks a save or publish on its own `[source-derived 2026-09-26 — utils/validators/opportunity-action-validators.ts:7-50]`. What does catch a missing stage is GHL's `validate-assets`, which answered "Referenced Pipeline Stage does not exist" on a nonexistent stage id (see [`a-trigger-filter-ghl-did-not-understand`](../../40-rules/a-trigger-filter-ghl-did-not-understand.md)).

`fields_referenced: ["pipeline_id", "pipeline_stage_id"]`.

`dripValidator` (length 778, result level `warning`). Per `sniffs/bundle/validators.json::dripValidator`:

```
if (batchSize <= 0 || batchSize > 10000)
  push { field: "batchSize", message: "drip_batch_size_invalid" }

const value = interval?.value
const unit  = interval?.timeUnit
if (!value || value <= 0)
  push { field: "interval.value", message: "drip_interval_required" }
else if (unit === "minutes" && value > 10080)
  push { field: "interval.value", message: "drip_interval_minutes_max" }
else if (unit === "hours"   && value > 168)
  push { field: "interval.value", message: "drip_interval_hours_max" }
else if (unit === "days"    && value > 7)
  push { field: "interval.value", message: "drip_interval_days_max" }
```

`fields_referenced: ["batchSize", "interval.value"]`.

`googleSheetsIntegrationValidator` (length 549, result level `warning`). Per `sniffs/bundle/validators.json::googleSheetsIntegrationValidator`:

```
const account = attributes.account
if (!account?.id) push { field: "oAuthId", message: "select_google_account" }
else {
  return [{
    url:  `${integrationsURL}/google/connections?locationId=${extras.locationId}`,
    method: "GET",
    absoluteUrl: true,
    headers: googleConnectionsHeaders(),
    transformResponse: (data) => {
      const connections = mapGoogleConnections(data.data)
      return connections.some(c => (c.altId ?? c.id) === account.id)
        ? []
        : { field: "oAuthId", message: "google_integration_not_valid" }
    }
  }]
}
```

Two distinct enforcements:

1. **`account.id` must be set** — otherwise emit `"select_google_account"`.
2. **The account id must exist in the location's connected Google integrations**, verified via a side `GET` to `/google/connections`. If not connected, emit `"google_integration_not_valid"`.

`fields_referenced: ["oAuthId"]` (a virtual field — the validator pushes the field name `oAuthId` even though the data lives under `attributes.account.id`).

`webhookValidator` (length 672, result level `warning`). Per `sniffs/bundle/validators.json::webhookValidator`:

```
if (!url || !url.trim())   push { field: "url",    message: "webhook_url_required" }
if (!method)               push { field: "method", message: "http_method_required" }
if (customData.some(row => !row.key?.trim() || row.value === null || row.value === undefined))
                           push { field: "customData", message: "custom_data_has_empty_fields" }
if (headers.some(row => !row.key?.trim() || row.value === null || row.value === undefined))
                           push { field: "headers",    message: "headers_has_empty_fields" }
```

`fields_referenced: ["customData", "headers", "method", "url"]`.

Empty arrays are OK; but each entry in a non-empty array must have a non-empty `key` and a defined `value` — the **validator** lets an empty-string `value` through (only `null`/`undefined` fail) `[source-derived 2026-09-26 — utils/validators/webhook-validators.ts:34-56]`. The **builder drawer is stricter**: it refuses to save a row with an empty `value` ("Empty field is not allowed", `emptyValues` tests `!data.value`) or a URL that fails its pattern (anything containing `{{` passes) `[source-derived 2026-09-29 — utils/validation.ts:68-82,179-186; models/actions/Webhook.ts:54-66]`.
